{"pack": "m2ui", "voice": "girl", "speaker": {"af_heart": 1.0}, "audio": "m2ui-20261117.mp4", "model": "Kokoro-82M v1.0 (Apache 2.0) via kokoro-onnx (MIT); misaki phonemizer (Apache 2.0)", "gap": 0.45, "clips": {"Chapter 3 complete! Talk to Mo at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [0.0, 4.404], "Mayor Bea is waiting for you on the beach. Go and say hello!": [4.854, 3.487], "Say hello to Gus the clockmaker, on the beach.": [8.791, 2.655], "Explore Port Lumen and meet its people.": [11.895, 2.441], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen. It starts at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [14.787, 4.937], "You learned it all! Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He heard something strange\u2026": [20.174, 4.191], "Someone is hiding up by the bells! Climb the ladder in the Clock Tower.": [24.815, 3.913], "Chapter 6 complete! Explore Port Lumen as much as you like.": [29.178, 3.913], "Help Rafi count his fish at the fish market. Count hundreds, tens and ones.": [33.541, 4.639], "Talk to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall: she has big news!": [38.63, 3.124], "Help Pedro count the people on his water taxi. He\u2019s on the Town Hall Plaza.": [42.204, 4.703], "Go see Gus in the Clock Tower. He found something!": [47.357, 3.081], "Chapter 4 complete! Now we know who sells the pages: the Crumb Crew!": [50.888, 4.255], "Chapter 5: why did the big clock stop?": [55.593, 2.612], "Chapter 5 complete! Someone took the Bell Gear to keep the bells quiet\u2026": [58.655, 4.468], "Chapter 6: who is hiding near the bells?": [63.573, 2.484], "The clock hand starts on 20. It jumps 3 tens to the right: 30, 40, 50.": [66.507, 5.62], "Count the hops: 1, 2, 3. Each hop is ten.": [72.577, 3.231], "It lands on 50! So 20 + 30 = 50.": [76.257, 3.615], "Now the hand goes back. It starts on 50 and jumps 2 tens to the LEFT: 40, 30.": [80.322, 5.94], "It lands on 30! Left means taking away: 50 \u2212 20 = 30.": [86.712, 5.108], "The hand can start between the marks, too. Start on 34 and jump 2 tens to the right: 44, 54.": [92.27, 7.241], "It lands on 54. Only the tens changed; the ones stay 4! So 34 + 20 = 54.": [99.961, 7.433], "Say hello to Mayor Bea in the Town Hall.": [107.845, 2.335], "Help Ms. Reyes read the new words on the Market Street signs!": [110.629, 3.465], "Lucy\u2019s robot fell apart on the Canal Walk. Help her build a new one!": [114.545, 4.276], "Help Captain Lin fill in her harbor book. She is on Museum Road.": [119.271, 3.785], "Walk the Tidewalk to Port Lumen! Start at the old dock, east of the lighthouse.": [123.506, 4.596], "Cross the Tidewalk! Mina is at the first rope bridge. Win her challenge.": [128.552, 4.447], "Cadet Jo guards the second rope bridge. Win the challenge to reach Port Lumen!": [133.449, 4.873], "Keep walking east. Port Lumen\u2019s beach is just ahead!": [138.772, 3.295], "Ruby is by the broken taxi dock at the harbor. Help her fix it!": [142.517, 4.084], "You have 5 planks! Stand by the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to lay each one.": [147.051, 4.703], "Leo is waiting by the Clock Tower. Help put the loose gears back!": [152.203, 3.892], "You have 5 gears! Go into the Clock Tower. Press A by the big wheels.": [156.545, 4.127], "One question for each thing you learned on Market Street. Each right answer gives you a plank!": [161.122, 5.257], "You have all the planks! Go to the Harbor taxi stop. Press A to build the dock.": [166.829, 4.425], "One question for each thing you learned on the Canal Walk. Each right answer gives you a gear!": [171.705, 5.279], "You have all the gears! Go into the Clock Tower and press A by the big wheels.": [177.433, 4.297], "Port Lumen stamps:": [182.181, 1.353], "Still to visit in Port Lumen:": [183.984, 1.908], "Find the people with a !": [186.342, 1.567], "A young otter with a red scarf steps out. {otter} jumps in front of you, fur up, with a little growl.": [188.359, 6.047], "Brioche stops. For a moment he just looks at {otter}.": [194.855, 3.316], "Hey, {otter} keeps looking into the water. Otters are great divers!": [198.621, 4.191], "Now {otter} can dive! Look for bubbles in the water near the shore.": [203.262, 3.977], "Brioche looks at {otter} one more time. He opens his mouth\u2026 then shuts it and runs off after the crew.": [207.689, 6.239], "Look, {name}! The tide went out! Now there is a path of sand across the sea!": [214.378, 3.892], "This is the Tidewalk. It goes all the way to Port Lumen. That's the city on Marlo's sea chart.": [218.72, 5.705], "Explorers come here at low tide. Two of them guard the rope bridges: win their challenge to cross!": [224.875, 5.961], "Their challenges review what we learned on the island. Don\u2019t worry: if you miss, you get help and try again.": [231.287, 6.303], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen \u2192 this way. Lighthouse Island \u2190 back across the dock. Walk only at low tide!": [238.039, 7.327], "THE TIDEWALK. Port Lumen, Old Town beach \u2192 right here. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the bridges.": [245.816, 7.647], "A tide pool! When the tide goes out, sea water stays behind in the low places.": [253.913, 4.937], "Little animals wait in the pools until the sea comes back. Look, but leave them in their home.": [259.3, 5.428], "A tiny lighthouse on Little Light islet. At night it blinks, so boats don't hit the hidden sand.": [265.178, 5.833], "Gulls are resting on Gull islet. Shh\u2026 let them sleep!": [271.461, 3.913], "Halt, explorer! I\u2019m Mina. I watch the sea birds of the Tidewalk with my binoculars.": [275.825, 5.428], "This rope bridge is mine to guard. To cross, win my review challenge!": [281.703, 4.511], "It has a bit of all you learned on the island!": [286.663, 2.356], "Yes, let\u2019s play!. Not now..": [289.469, 1.78], "The bridge is open, {name}! Want to play again, just for fun?": [291.699, 3.103], "You remember so much! Here is a Tidewalk sticker for your notebook. The bridge is open!": [295.252, 5.087], "Hey, explorer! I\u2019m Milo. My kite flies best on the sandbars!": [300.789, 4.169], "Want a math challenge? Adding and taking away, up to 20. It\u2019s just for fun, you can say no!": [305.408, 6.025], "My kite is still up! Another math challenge?": [311.883, 2.719], "Wow, you\u2019re quick! Take a Tidewalk sticker!": [315.052, 2.335], "Hello, dear. I\u2019m Grandma Opal. I paint the tide pools while the sea is away.": [317.837, 5.023], "Do you like stories and words? Try my reading challenge. Only if you want to!": [323.309, 4.703], "Back for more words, dear? Another reading challenge?": [328.462, 3.039], "What a fine reader! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. I painted it myself.": [331.951, 4.212], "Shh\u2026 a crab! Oh, hi! I\u2019m Finn. I look for animals in the tide pools.": [336.613, 5.108], "Want a challenge about science and maps? Land and water, nature, and places! You can say no.": [342.171, 5.983], "Found anything in the pools? Want another science and maps challenge?": [348.603, 3.785], "You know your land and water! Here is a Tidewalk sticker!": [352.839, 3.188], "Ahoy! I\u2019m Cadet Jo of the coast watch. I keep the Tidewalk safe.": [356.477, 4.063], "To cross my bridge, show me what you learned on the island. Story problems too: first to 5 points!": [360.989, 6.281], "Miss on your first try and I get a point. Ready?": [367.721, 3.017], "The way to Port Lumen is open, {name}! Want to play again?": [371.188, 3.017], "Well done, explorer! Here is a Tidewalk sticker. The bridge is open: Port Lumen is just ahead!": [374.655, 5.919], "THE TIDEWALK. Low tide! Port Lumen \u2192 across the sand and the rope bridges.": [381.024, 5.108], "THE OLD DOCK. At high tide there is only sea here. At low tide\u2026 who knows?": [386.582, 4.575], "THE TIDEWALK. Lighthouse Island \u2190 across the sand and the rope bridges. Walk only at low tide!": [391.607, 6.644], "{name}, you beat all five Tidewalk explorers!": [398.701, 2.42], "That\u2019s the gold Tidewalk sticker! Look for it in your notebook, next to your treasures.": [401.571, 4.553], "Gus (in the Clock Tower)": [406.574, 1.588], "Gus in the Clock Tower": [408.612, 1.567], "Mayor Bea (in the Town Hall)": [410.629, 1.716], "Mayor Bea in the Town Hall": [412.795, 1.567], "Pedro (by the Town Hall Plaza)": [414.811, 2.121], "Pedro by the Town Hall Plaza": [417.383, 2.015], "Captain Lin (in the Harbor Office)": [419.847, 2.143], "Captain Lin in the Harbor Office": [422.44, 2.036], "Rafi (at the fish market by the harbor)": [424.926, 2.399], "Rafi at the fish market by the harbor": [427.775, 2.271], "Coco (in the Ice Cream Parlor)": [430.495, 2.036], "Coco in the Ice Cream Parlor": [432.981, 1.951], "Pepper (in the Galleria)": [435.382, 1.481], "Pepper in the Galleria": [437.313, 1.396], "Mr. Fitz (in the Galleria)": [439.159, 1.823], "Mr. Fitz in the Galleria": [441.432, 1.673], "Dr. Kai (in the City Aquarium)": [443.555, 2.271], "Dr. Kai in the City Aquarium": [446.276, 2.185], "Ms. Reyes (in the City Library)": [448.911, 2.1], "Ms. Reyes in the City Library": [451.461, 2.036], "Dr. Amara (in the Museum)": [453.947, 2.079], "Dr. Amara in the Museum": [456.476, 1.972], "Olive (in the greenhouse, City Park)": [458.898, 2.335], "Olive in the greenhouse, City Park": [461.683, 2.185], "Mr. Bloom (on Market Street)": [464.318, 1.993], "Mr. Bloom on Market Street": [466.761, 1.844], "Lucy (on Canal Row)": [469.055, 1.716], "Lucy on Canal Row": [471.221, 1.481], "Grandpa Walt (in the Old Town square)": [473.153, 2.42], "Grandpa Walt in the Old Town square": [476.023, 2.164], "Mr. Bloom (at home tonight (look for the ! on a door))": [478.637, 2.996], "Mr. Bloom at home tonight (look for the ! on a door)": [482.083, 2.932], "Lucy (at home tonight (look for the ! on a door))": [485.465, 2.783], "Lucy at home tonight (look for the ! on a door)": [488.697, 2.761], "Grandpa Walt (at home tonight (look for the ! on a door))": [491.909, 3.252], "Grandpa Walt at home tonight (look for the ! on a door)": [495.611, 3.039], "Pedro (at home tonight (look for the ! on a door))": 